From 71073db965cd363f353f956551f872f204a87838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:15:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] A voice contract says what its agreement says of
 commission, and the office's answer is shown to read its keenness

The review's two blocking findings. Every voice part's contract still said voice-over was outside an agent's agreement
and owed no commission, while the pay took ten percent under an agreement that covers voice-over. The clause is now made
from the agreement the engagement is made under, by the pay's own rule (owedAgreement, then coveredUnder): commission
owed where the terms take voice-over in, the reason none is where they leave it out, and no clause when nobody
represented the actor, as on any other contract. And no test proved the answer to an ask depends on how keen the office
is: the journeys drew under every chance or over every chance, so an answer ignoring the stored chance passed. A twin
now does it: a life whose draw falls between the chance as things stand and the chance with a day missed on its record,
agreed in one and kept in the other, each at the chance its panel shows.

From the should-fix and note findings, decided rather than deferred because each was cheap and clearly right:
- A festival introduction names the entry's own festival (institutionById), not Sundance whatever the entry, and says a
  film was in the official selection until it has screened; the work the office has to go on says the same.
- The guide's agreement entry ends it "when its term is up", not its year, and the new entry's example states its
  result as a chance, worked from TERMS, rather than as certain.
- DealVersion's how and ask and the festival introductions' moment went: nothing read them, and the version's number,
  the agreement's ask and the introduction's via say each.
- The industry reference lists an agency's other departments, so Celia Brannock no longer sits under a page that names
  only the legit one; the slate-reach decider samples a part's reach as reachOf gives it; voice-over added to a legit
  agreement is handled by the agent with the voice-over department, as the submission it makes says; and a real
  agent's answer, on the notice and the Terms panel, says the agency's pages give no terms, so it's the game's.
- The older-save test loads the save and plays the ask and the term to its end, as the review's probe did.

The festival route still waits on the festivals cluster's call, which is that cluster's and the integration's.

